  fall asleep which is probably more of  like a nervous anxiety habit than an  actual  need to go most nights these days when  i put my book down because my eyes are  droopy and i turn off the lights  i can pretty much go right to sleep  which is great but  sometimes i get in my head  and i lay there and i think what if i  don't sleep  how long have i been laying here uh if  it's been 20 minutes my therapist said i  should get out of bed so i don't poison  my bed  maybe i need to pee a little bit if i  don't go i'll just wake up again  maybe i'm a little bit hungry and i  should go have a snack oh now i'm  thirsty now i have to pee  blah blah blah blah blah so a few  nights of the week i end up having to  get up  and do something in another room  recently i've gotten into the annoying  habit of  walking on the treadmill and watching  some light tv to kind of like  reset my anxious brain this is not like  a hit session  this is a pretty leisurely slow walk but  i  almost see it as like a walking  meditation because sometimes if i'm  too still as i am in my bed my mind just  doesn't slow down  so i see it as being better to move my  body  so that my mind can get to rest this is  also not the best time for like my  beloved true crime shows i've made that  mistake in the past and it has haunted  me as i tried to get back to sleep  i try to keep it really light and boring  with like jeopardy  or wheel of fortune something that feels  kind of geriatric  which i guess reminds me of sleep sorry  grams  so after doing like 30 to 60 minutes of  something like that  i'm usually calm enough to try again and  usually  i am able to fall asleep but then i do  have to get up at like 1 30 in the  morning to pump  and usually i can fall back asleep but  it is  also short-lived if i do because well  you guys know  i'm an early bird yep you read that  right  4am partially by obligation partially by  choice but i mean  i don't know if i had my way i would  love to sleep until six  love 